WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.491 --> 00:00:11.923
What is the world's most popular drink? What drink has played an important role in the world's history, politics, and religion?

2
00:00:11.924 --> 00:00:14.701
What drink is over five thousand years old?

3
00:00:14.702 --> 00:00:23.874
The answer is tea, and its story begins with Chinese Emperor Shen Nung, a scholar and scientist who lived over five thousand years ago.

4
00:00:23.875 --> 00:00:29.922
The emperor had ruled that throughout his kingdom all drinking water must be boiled as a hygienic precaution.

5
00:00:29.923 --> 00:00:37.068
One day while visiting a distant region, the emperor stopped to rest, and the servants began to boil water for everyone to drink.

6
00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:42.815
At this moment, the wind blew and some dried leaves from a nearby bush fell into the boiling water.

7
00:00:42.816 --> 00:00:44.768
The liquid became brown.

8
00:00:44.769 --> 00:00:50.949
As a scientist, the emperor was interested in the new liquid, drank some, and found it very refreshing.

9
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:57.168
The tree was a wild tea tree. And so, according to legend, tea was created.

10
00:00:57.169 --> 00:01:01.057
From ancient times tea was renowned as a healthy, refreshing drink.

11
00:01:01.058 --> 00:01:05.593
The first detailed description of tea was written in 350 AD.

12
00:01:05.594 --> 00:01:09.783
Fresh, green tea leaves were picked, then pressed into hard "bricks."

13
00:01:09.784 --> 00:01:15.600
These bricks were roasted, crumbled into water, and boiled with onion, ginger, and orange.

14
00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:22.752
It was not until the Tang Dynasty that tea became China's national drink and the word "cha" was used to describe tea.

15
00:01:22.753 --> 00:01:28.860
The first book on tea, called Cha Ching, was written by Lu Yu in 780 AD.

16
00:01:28.861 --> 00:01:34.034
It had three volumes and described tea cultivation and preparation in ancient China.

17
00:01:34.035 --> 00:01:41.200
The modern term "tea" derives from words such as tchai, cha, and tay in early Chinese dialects.

18
00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:44.414
Its botanical name is Camellia sinensis.

19
00:01:44.415 --> 00:01:48.905
Tea is an evergreen plant with smooth, shiny, pointed leaves.

20
00:01:48.906 --> 00:01:54.015
After China, the first two countries to adopt tea were its neighbors, Korea and Japan.

21
00:01:54.016 --> 00:02:01.164
Tea first came to Korea during the Unified Shilla Dynasty, between 57 BC and 935 AD.

22
00:02:01.165 --> 00:02:06.122
As it was in China, tea was used for social and religious purposes in Korea.

23
00:02:06.123 --> 00:02:13.376
Tea was drunk socially among the royal family and aristocrats, and Buddhist monks drank tea to help them stay awake during meditation.

24
00:02:13.377 --> 00:02:16.773
Tea drinking became widespread in the Goryo Dynasty.

25
00:02:16.774 --> 00:02:23.981
During this time, special ceramic cups and bowls for tea drinking were designed, and an elaborate tea ceremony was developed.

26
00:02:23.982 --> 00:02:31.248
The ceremony begins with pouring the boiling water into a bowl, where it stands until it cools to about 60 degrees Celsius.

27
00:02:31.249 --> 00:02:34.493
If the water is too hot, the tea will be too bitter.

28
00:02:34.494 --> 00:02:40.239
The teapot and cups are warmed with some of the water, and then the tea leaves are warmed in the teapot.

29
00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:44.858
Then, the water is poured into the teapot and left to brew for two or three minutes.

30
00:02:44.859 --> 00:02:51.126
When the tea is poured, each cup is filled little by little so that the taste is evenly distributed in all the cups.

31
00:02:51.127 --> 00:03:02.606
The tea must be sipped slowly, and as you sip, you must think about the four characteristics of tea according to Korean Buddhism: peacefulness, respectfulness, purity, and quietness.

32
00:03:02.607 --> 00:03:10.647
During the Joseon Dynasty, Confucianism replaced Buddhism as the court religion, and wine replaced tea as the favored drink.

33
00:03:10.648 --> 00:03:15.107
Tea went out of fashion and was not revived until five hundred years later.

34
00:03:15.108 --> 00:03:21.829
Tea was introduced to Japan in 1191 by Yeisei, "The Father of Tea," a traveling Buddhist monk.

35
00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:28.164
As in Korea, tea was first used by Buddhist monks and aristocrats, and then spread to the rest of society.

36
00:03:28.165 --> 00:03:32.101
By this time, tea was no longer served in "cakes" but was powdered.

37
00:03:32.102 --> 00:03:35.982
Tea became so popular that even a tea guessing game was played.

38
00:03:35.983 --> 00:03:45.087
Beginning in early morning and continuing well into evening, guests would sample as many as fifty varieties of tea, trying to guess their places of origin.

39
00:03:45.088 --> 00:03:49.706
From the fourteenth to sixteenth centuries, a Japanese tea ritual was developed.

40
00:03:49.707 --> 00:03:57.907
The Japanese tea ceremony takes place in a special room designed for tea drinking and consists of many small rituals that have to be learned by heart.

41
00:03:57.908 --> 00:04:03.588
It is much more elaborate than the Korean ceremony, and almost every hand movement is prescribed.

42
00:04:03.589 --> 00:04:06.644
Tea didn't reach Europe until the fifteenth century.

43
00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:11.508
As the Europeans increased their trade with China, rumors of a new substance circulated.

44
00:04:11.509 --> 00:04:15.284
When tea finally arrived, people were unsure how to use it.

45
00:04:15.285 --> 00:04:20.113
One writer suggested that tea leaves be boiled, salted, buttered, and eaten!

46
00:04:20.114 --> 00:04:24.728
Some doctors and scholars also warned that this strange dark liquid was unhealthy.

47
00:04:24.729 --> 00:04:28.876
In reality, tea drinking actually increased the health of people in Europe.

48
00:04:28.877 --> 00:04:34.277
Water was too dangerous to drink at the time, so people drank beer at breakfast, lunch, and dinner!

49
00:04:34.278 --> 00:04:39.934
Tea, made with boiled and therefore safe water, was a vast improvement in the European diet.

50
00:04:39.935 --> 00:04:45.695
Nowadays, black tea is Britain's national drink, but Britons were the last Europeans to adopt it.

51
00:04:45.696 --> 00:04:52.528
Within fifty years, however, tea became so popular in Britain that Britain was the largest tea importer in Europe.

52
00:04:52.529 --> 00:04:57.741
Over the next few centuries, tea played a major role in world history and politics.

53
00:04:57.742 --> 00:05:01.083
European companies bought tea from China and India.

54
00:05:01.084 --> 00:05:07.738
The East India Company, in fact, became so rich and powerful that it ruled the nation of India for several years.

55
00:05:07.739 --> 00:05:14.286
This British company forced Indian workers to produce the drug opium, which was sold to China in exchange for tea.

56
00:05:14.287 --> 00:05:25.054
In the 1800s, England was the largest drug trafficking organization in the world, and was responsible for a devastating drug addiction problem in China—all just to control the trade in tea.

57
00:05:25.055 --> 00:05:28.932
In the new colony of America, tea was also causing trouble.

58
00:05:28.933 --> 00:05:37.152
In 1773, in a famous incident called the Boston Tea Party, 340 chests of tea were emptied into the ocean.

59
00:05:37.153 --> 00:05:46.712
Residents of Boston were protesting against the same company, the East India Company, and their protest was one of the first incidents that led to the American Revolution.

60
00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:53.255
In the nineteenth century, tea led to the creation of two new meal times: "morning tea" and "afternoon tea."

61
00:05:53.256 --> 00:05:59.755
A woman who managed a bread shop in England convinced her bosses to allow her to serve tea to her favorite customers.

62
00:05:59.756 --> 00:06:05.081
The shop set up some tables in 1864 and a new form of socializing was born.

63
00:06:05.082 --> 00:06:11.421
As one famous author said, "For the English, afternoon tea is really a picnic indoors."

64
00:06:11.422 --> 00:06:16.523
Morning tea and afternoon tea are still common in Britain and Commonwealth countries.

65
00:06:16.524 --> 00:06:24.616
Iced green tea was served with alcohol in the United States in the 1800s, but it was not until 1904 that iced tea really took off.

66
00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:28.336
At the World's Fair, hot tea was given away free for guests.

67
00:06:28.337 --> 00:06:33.223
Because of the intense heat, ice was added to the tea and it became an instant hit!

68
00:06:33.224 --> 00:06:37.779
Today, iced tea is usually made with lemon and sweetened with sugar.

69
00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:42.267
Nowadays, tea comes in green, black, and oolong varieties.

70
00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:50.923
Europeans and Americans have traditionally favored black teas, Asians prefer green tea, and Indians and East Asians drink a spiced tea called chai.

71
00:06:50.924 --> 00:06:58.096
However, the health benefits of green tea, including reducing the risks of cancer, are increasing its popularity worldwide.

72
00:06:58.097 --> 00:07:05.646
Herbal "tea," sometimes called a tisane or an infusion, is made by infusing herbs other than the tea plant in hot water.

73
00:07:05.647 --> 00:07:09.296
Hundreds of different kinds of herbal tea are drunk around the world.

74
00:07:09.297 --> 00:07:14.474
Some of the most popular are chamomile, mint, rosehip, and ginger.

75
00:07:14.475 --> 00:07:23.087
Many blends of real tea are prepared by adding other plants; for example, the popular Earl Grey tea is black tea infused with bergamot.

76
00:07:23.088 --> 00:07:27.023
Tea has been a part of human culture since the earliest written records.

77
00:07:27.024 --> 00:07:32.184
It has shaped societies, started wars, and changed the course of history.

78
00:07:32.185 --> 00:07:34.335
All because of a simple drink!

79
00:07:34.336 --> 00:07:49.000
William Gladstone, the prime minister of England, summed it up nicely: "If you are cold, tea will warm you; if you are too heated; it will cool you; if you are depressed, it will cheer you; if you are exhausted, it will calm you."
